# Trivy filesystem-scan exceptions (applies to `trivy fs .` in CI).
# Each entry must keep its justification comment: no silent ignores.

# CVE-2026-93687 (braces via micromatch <- http-proxy-middleware, gateway):
# no patched version exists upstream (affected <= 3.0.3, fixed: none).
# The matched patterns are static server-side proxy route config, never
# attacker-controlled input, so the stack-exhaustion path is unreachable.
CVE-2026-93687

# CVE-2026-41907 (uuid via exceljs, frontend): missing buffer-bounds check
# triggers only when buf is passed to v3/v5/v6; exceljs never does. No
# non-breaking upgrade path (exceljs 4.4.0 already latest).
CVE-2026-41907

# GO-2026-5932 (golang.org/x/crypto, transitive-only via lms-service):
# no fixed version published; package is not directly imported.
GO-2026-5932
